{"id": "29800", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=29800", "title": "River Edge", "text": "River Edge is in New Jersey.\nUnderstand.\nRiver Edge is a borough in Bergen County, New Jersey. River Edge was incorporated on June 30, 1894.\nGet in.\nFrom Exit 161 on the Garden State Parkway North or Rt. 17, travel about 2 miles on Route 4 East, take the exit for Hackensack Ave. North / River Edge.\nFrom Route 4, take the exit for Hackensack Ave. North / River Edge.\nGet around.\nYou can get around by car, bike, bus, train, or walking.\nEat.\nAll of these places are on Kinderkamack Avenue."}
{"id": "29801", "revid": "195012", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=29801", "title": "River Falls", "text": "River Falls is a city in Northwest Wisconsin.\nUnderstand.\nRiver Falls is an international destination for kayaking and fly fishing with visitors from all over the world. The Kinnickinnic River, nicknamed \"Kinni Creek\" is a class 1 trout stream that boasts of 6,000-8,000 trout per mile. German Brown Trout and Brook trout are the species that you will find there. The city is also home to the University of Wisconsin at River Falls, which also has many international visitors. The industrial park is home to many international businesses as well. "}
