{"id": "29972", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=29972", "title": "Rolla (Missouri)", "text": "Rolla is a city in the Central Missouri region of Missouri on historic Route 66. It is home to Missouri University of Science and Technology (Formerly University of Missouri at Rolla) campus.\nUnderstand.\nRolla is a beautiful town located along I-44, with a population of about 20,000.\nGet in.\nBy car.\nRolla is about 1 hour and 45 minutes to both Springfield to the west and St. Louis to the east along Interstate 44. Columbia, MO is 1 hour and 45 minutes North of Rolla. You can take US 63 from Columbia.\nBy plane.\nThe closest large commercial airport is Lambert St. Louis International Airport which is served by most US carriers. The airport is about 1 hour and 45 minutes from the city. Greyhound and USA Express have shuttles from the airport to Rolla and back or you can rent a car at the airport.\nFor private aircraft Rolla National Airport is about a 15 minute drive north of the city.\nYou can fly into Waynesville - St. Robert Regional Airport from St Louis.\nBy bus.\nNote: Greyhound no longer stops into St Roberts and/or Fort Leonardwood. Nearest Greyhound station/stop is in Greyhound. They travel on I-44 between St Louis and Oklahoma City via Springfield, Joplin and Tulsa.\nBy train.\nThe nearest train station is the Jefferson City Amtrak Station. From there you can rent a car. You can also take a train to St. Louis Gateway station.\nGet around.\nNo public transportation exists in Rolla and a car is almost a necessity to get around. However, bicycling is a viable alternative and the town is small enough walking could be facilitated if necessary. There are a couple of taxi cab companies in town also.\nYou can take an Uber but there is usually only one or two available."}
